apart. Can we tell the difference between temperamental shyness, cultural shyness, and then shyness that it's a reflection of previous difficult events? And based on what you previously said about temperament, it would seem that temperamental shyness would be the one that is most innate and not changeable. It's less changeable. I think one of the things we try to say about temperament, it is clay. And clay is more. moldable. And you can shape something out of clay based on the culture, based on parenting, based on relationships with peers. And so it's not always going to look the same. However,

