have a mix of the bold and the bashful. And it's that mix over the centuries that allows that species to survive. The bold and the bashful humans allow our society to survive. We need both. So just to wrap up, question I like to ask at the end is, what are you working on now? What are the big questions that you're trying to answer? One of the things we know about the biology of temperament is based on tasks and situations that we contrive in the laboratory. So, for example, for the young child, the infant, we might bring out the jack in the box. And you have some children that are just thrilled by the jack-in-box. Some are terrified.

